<title>JAPAN: L-Bank launches 3.0% yen/A$ reverse samurai-Nomura.</title>
<headline>L-Bank launches 3.0% yen/A$ reverse samurai-Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar reverse dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Landeskreditbank Baden-Wuerttemberg (L-Bank)</p>
<p> AMT		 20 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.0 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  24 April 2007</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 101.00</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  24 April 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 11 (scheduled)</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa, IBCA AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTES: The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,202.91 to 500,000 yen. The coupon will be paid in Australian dollars, while redemption will be in yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
